thread.content:
The feedback has two distinct signals: (1) a possible render regression (white screen), and (2) overall visual quality is far below the "award-winning" bar. Round 001 was the same feedback that timed out — this is a re-submission, so action is needed.

```json
{
  "form": "mutation_list",
  "rationale": "Address the user's two concerns: triage the white-screen render regression as urgent blocking work, and raise the visual-quality bar with a dedicated design-elevation item plus a references study, since the existing theming-engine item is scaffolding-level and won't on its own produce award-winning results.",
  "mutations": [
    {
      "id": "m1",
      "op": "add_item",
      "item": {
        "kind": "execute",
        "name": "command-center-render-triage",
        "title": "Diagnose and fix command-center white-screen / render regression",
        "description": "User reports the command-center UI may currently render as a blank white screen. Reproduce the failure (browser devtools console, network tab, vite build output), identify the root cause (likely candidates: missing route component, broken import, R3F/Three.js init crash, CSS that hides content, or a runtime error in one of the 6 page components), and ship a fix. Acceptance: every route under /mission-control, /hive, /forge, /ledger, /broadcast, /panorama renders non-empty content with no console errors in a fresh browser session, both in `vrooli scenario start command-center` dev mode and in a vite production build. Add a smoke test (Playwright or equivalent) that loads each route and asserts non-blank content so this regression cannot silently recur.",
        "priority": 1,
        "effort": "S",
        "depends_on": ["execute/command-center-scenario-scaffold"]
      },
      "rationale": "User explicitly flagged 'might have issues preventing it from rendering at all (just seeing white)'. Nothing else in this initiative matters until the app renders. Tagged P1 and S so it gets picked up immediately."
    },
    {
      "id": "m2",
      "op": "add_item",
      "item": {
        "kind": "research",
        "name": "command-center-visual-design-references",
        "title": "Curate visual references and design language for award-winning dashboards",
        "description": "Compile a concrete reference deck for each of the 6 themes (Ground Control, Bioluminescent, Foundry, Vault, Signal Tower, Cosmos) drawing from Awwwards/FWA/CSSDA dashboard winners, sci-fi UI work (Territory Studio: Blade Runner 2049, The Martian, Oblivion), generative-art studios (Active Theory, Resn, Hello Monday), and data-viz showcases (Pitch Interactive, Stamen). Output: a markdown brief per theme with 5–10 reference images/links, a typography pairing, a color/material palette beyond CSS variables (gradients, noise, glass, glow, grain), motion principles, and a 'one signature hero element' that makes the page memorable. This brief becomes the visual spec the theming-engine and per-page work executes against.",
        "priority": 2,
        "effort": "S",
        "depends_on": []
      },
      "rationale": "The current architecture research is structural (R3F + CSS vars + Recharts). 'Award-winning' is a visual-language problem, not an architecture problem — without a concrete reference brief, the theming-engine work will keep producing competent-but-generic output."
    },
    {
      "id": "m3",
      "op": "add_item",
      "item": {
        "kind": "execute",
        "name": "command-center-visual-polish-pass",
        "title": "Visual elevation pass: take all 6 pages from functional to award-winning",
        "description": "After the theming engine and kiosk UX land, do a dedicated quality pass that pushes each of the 6 pages to portfolio-grade. Per page: implement the signature hero element from the references brief, add layered depth (R3F scene + foreground UI + grain/glass overlays), tune typography (variable fonts, optical sizing, generous tracking for kiosk distance), add micro-motion (number tickers, ambient particle drift, hover/focus states even though kiosk has no hover — use auto-cycle highlights instead), ensure every panel has intentional negative space, and remove anything that looks like a default Recharts/MUI/Tailwind look. Acceptance: side-by-side compare each page against its references brief; an unbiased reviewer would call the result 'designed' rather than 'styled'. Capture before/after screenshots in the item folder.",
        "priority": 2,
        "effort": "L",
        "depends_on": [
          "execute/command-center-theming-engine",
          "execute/command-center-kiosk-ux",
          "research/command-center-visual-design-references"
        ]
      },
      "rationale": "User said even before the render bug it 'looked bad'. The existing theming-engine item builds the system; this item is the actual aesthetic execution against that system. Splitting the two prevents 'theming engine works = visual goal achieved' false-completion."
    },
    {
      "id": "m4",
      "op": "change_priority",
      "target": "execute/command-center-theming-engine",
      "priority": 1,
      "rationale": "Per-page visual identity is the stated differentiator of the entire initiative; bumping from P2 to P1 reflects that and gets it queued right after the render fix."
    },
    {
      "id": "m5",
      "op": "update_item",
      "target": "execute/command-center-theming-engine",
      "fields": {
        "description_append": "\n\n---\n**Visual quality bar (added from feedback round 002):** Output must be evaluated against the references brief produced by `research/command-center-visual-design-references`. Generic CSS-variable swap across pages is insufficient — each theme must include a per-page R3F scene, a signature visual element, and typography/material choices that make the page recognizable from a thumbnail. Land Mission Control as a fully realized vertical slice before generalizing to the remaining 5 pages."
      },
      "rationale": "Existing item description risks being interpreted as 'wire up CSS variables and ship'. User feedback makes clear that bar is too low; appending the explicit quality criteria keeps the item honest without rewriting it."
    }
  ]
}
```
